  "answer_text": "While MSNBC is a premium cable news channel that typically requires a pay-TV subscription or a paid live TV streaming package to watch the full 24/7 video feed, there are several **legal ways to stream it for free** or through temporary free trials. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Trials on Live TV Streaming Services (Temporary Free Video)\nIf you need to watch a live broadcast right now (such as a major breaking news event or election coverage), you can sign up for a free trial with a live TV streaming service. Just remember to cancel before the trial ends to avoid being charged.\n\n*   **FuboTV:** Offers a **7-day free trial** that includes MSNBC. \n*   **DirecTV Stream:** Frequently offers a **5-day free trial** and carries MSNBC in its basic \"Entertainment\" package.\n*   **YouTube TV:** Often offers a **7- to 14-day free trial** for new users.\n*   **Hulu + Live TV:** Occasionally offers short free trial promotions (usually 3 days).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Stream Live MSNBC Audio 24/7 (100% Free)\nIf you don't need to physically watch the TV screen and just want to listen to the news, **you can stream the live, real-time audio broadcast of MSNBC for free** without any subscriptions.\n*   **TuneIn Radio:** You can listen to the live MSNBC audio stream (which sometimes displays under the rebranded name **MS NOW**) for free via the TuneIn app or website. \n*   **The MS NOW / MSNBC App:** The official app has a \"Listen\" tab that allows you to stream live audio of the broadcast and select shows for free without logging in.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Watch Free On-Demand Clips & Highlights\nWhile the 24/7 live video stream is locked behind a paywall, you can watch individual segments, highlight clips, and complete breakdowns of major shows like *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, and *The Beat with Ari Melber* for free.\n*   **The MSNBC YouTube Channel:** Free, near-instant uploads of major show segments and breaking news clips are posted throughout the day.\n*   **MSNBC.com / MS NOW App:** Both platforms offer free video clips and articles of the day's top opinions and news stories without requiring a TV provider login.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Free Alternative: NBC News NOW\nIf you just want live, high-quality, rolling national and international news coverage from the same parent organization, you can watch **NBC News NOW**. \n*   Unlike MSNBC, NBC News NOW is a **100% free, 24/7 live streaming news channel**. \n*   It is available on free services like Pluto TV, Tubi, Samsung TV Plus, Roku Channel, Freevee, and directly on the NBC News website and app without any login or subscription. *(Note: While it features top-tier reporting, it does not carry MSNBC's specific host-led primetime opinion programs).*",
